# Throwaway browser profiles from QA runs — never commit these,
# they carry cookies and saved logins.
.qa/

# The demo film is developed locally and is not part of the judged repository.
# 6.7 GB of rendered frames and source live here; the finished MP4 is uploaded
# to the submission directly.
film/

# Local screen-recording playbook (README/SCRIPT/SHOTLIST for the submission
# video). Working notes for the humans on camera, not part of the judged
# repository.
DEMO/

# Tesseract OCR language data. tesseract.js writes this to the working
# directory of whatever process invokes it locally; the OCR path
# (web/src/components/bill/capture.tsx) loads it on demand from tesseract.js's
# own CDN/package paths at runtime, so nothing in the repo needs a bundled copy.
*.traineddata

# Internal working documents. These are for the team, not for judges:
# AUDIT.md scores our own weaknesses, TASKS.md is an unfinished work queue,
# HACKATHON.md is submission strategy, PITCH.md is internal messaging discipline.
AUDIT.md
TASKS.md
docs/HACKATHON.md
docs/PITCH.md

# Presenter notes and the exported deck. /deck serves the same slides live and
# can print its own PDF, so neither needs to ship; the script is rehearsal-only.
docs/PITCH_DECK_SCRIPT.md
docs/Sutra-Pitch-Deck.pdf
